            <ArticleTitle>[Implantation of an inverse prosthesis after management of an infected subcapital humerus fracture initially treated with osteosynthesis].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>765-6, 768-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>After repeated failure of osteosynthesis of a subcapital humerus fracture, the humeral joint got infected. Radical surgery, use of a temporary Palacos-Refobacin spacer, and secondary implantation of an inverse prosthesis achieved painlessness and satisfying functional results.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
